desc:EON: Quezy
// Quezy -- a free EQ that matches ReEQ everywhere (EON Studios). Spec: .docs/specs/Spec_Quezy_Free_EQ_2026-10-10.md
// BUILD STEPS 1 + 4a + 4b + 4c + 1b + 2 + 3 (2026-10-20/22): 16 bands, all 17 shapes, slopes 6..120 dB/oct, per-band placement
// (stereo / mid / side / left / right), the output section (gains, mid-side or left-right, polarities, Scale,
// Limit), and the window (qz_face.jsfx-inc): the curve graph with ReEQ's gestures, the band bar, the band
// editor and the output bar. 4b: listen (Shift at the pointer, a headphones button per band) and the house theme
// (the whole window follows the suite theme, the graph too; NATIVE = Quezy's own Midnight look). 4c: a strip shows
// the curve and its dots drag. 1b: the filters keep their analogue shape up to the top of the range (matched
// coefficients; ReEQ's bilinear ones squash the top octave). 0.6.0: the window's lines grow with it; narrow bands are drawn to
// their real depth (each band with a Q adds points where its curve turns fastest); ReEQ's own habits the port had missed
// (a cut made by double-click takes its Q from the click height, frequency reset to 500 Hz, ctrl-drag of a selected dot,
// the box selecting live, the editor moving on after a delete, shape changes resetting the slope, a Bypassed band's
// outline, stems from dots to their curves, dots hidden while the pointer is away, cents in the readouts, the version
// in the graph menu, placement marks on the dots, a total curve per placement); a line pattern per placement; the
// strip draws each band's fill. 0.7.0: auto gain (step 2: ReEQ's, over a steadier 2 s window, and its SET bake).
// 0.8.0 (step 3): nothing steps the sound any more: a change of shape, slope, placement, Mode or stereo mode glides
// or crossfades (ReEQ clicks on all of them); there is no HQ (2x) mode, the matched filters already match ReEQ's HQ with
// no latency (the user: "Drop it"). 0.8.1: the looks: the graph menu's Window look and Strip look pick the bands'
// fill / lines / both and the dots' numbered ring / plain / numbered badge, each saved with the instance; the dots are
// drawn by the library (rk_curve), whose Badge is Quezy's dot now. 0.9.0 (step 5): the analyser (ReEQ's spectrum
// library as rk_spectrum, its source / display / range / tilt / window / FFT size / pre-EQ trace / peaks / piano
// options in the graph menu, plus a decay speed, a freeze and the phase curve; the listen trace while a listen plays;
// the strips show it too, switchable; nothing is analysed while no window or strip is on screen). 0.9.1 (step 6, part 1): the native looks Carbon, Aurora,
// Ember, Paper (warm off-white) and White beside Midnight (the graph menu's Native look). 0.9.2 (step 6, part 2): link
// groups (the house gear, badge and group grid, sliders 1-218) and the grid's ACTIVE pills. 0.9.3 (step 7): the locked
// drag, Split L/R, Copy / Paste, undo / redo, A / B, typed values, hover help, the level-matched BYPASS and the factory
// presets (Quezy_ReaKit.jsfx.rpl). Not yet: the release checks (step 8); dynamics are release 2
// (their controls exist, hidden and inert, so release 2 never moves a saved value).
// DSP: Simper SVF via rk_svf.jsfx-inc (ReEQ's svf_filter) + rk_svf_match.jsfx-inc (magnitude-matched coefficients,
//      Ivantsov's maps, MIT) + qz_engine.jsfx-inc (band objects, ReEQ's shape dispatch and per-band mid/side
//      placement, Quezy's own Flat Tilt / Flat Gain / Bell Prop Q).
// Version: 1.0.1 (2026-11-04: a Quezy shown in the track panel AND the mixer no longer blinks). 1.0.0 (2026-11-04, the first release in ReaKit FX). Before it, 0.9.3 (skeleton + window 4a + listen and theme 4b + the strip's draggable dots 4c + matched filters 1b + the
// window's lines, narrow bands and ReEQ's missing habits + auto gain 2 + click-free switching 3 + the looks + the
// analyser 5 + the native looks and link groups 6 + the extras 7; 1.0.0 at release). Keep #qz_ver in @init in step.
//tags: equalizer filter parametric shelf mid-side
//author: EON Studios; SVF engine and band design: Justin Johnson (ReEQ, MIT); matched coefficients after Yuriy Ivantsov (MIT)
// (C) 2026 EON Studios. Quezy's own code (this file, qz_face.jsfx-inc, qz_engine.jsfx-inc): EON Free Licence 1.0: free
// to use in any work; not for sale, redistribution or reuse of its code (LICENSE-EON-FREE.md; the user, 2026-10-30,
// over MIT: "that means someone could sell it"). The parts after Justin Johnson's and Yuriy Ivantsov's work keep their
// MIT licences, whose notices follow.
//
// ---- Justin Johnson, ReEQ 1.2.0 (engine, shape dispatch, per-band placement) ----
// MIT License
//
// Copyright (c) Justin Johnson
//
// Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
// of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
// in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
// to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
// copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
// furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:
//
// The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
// copies or substantial portions of the Software.
//
// THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
// IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
// FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
// AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
// LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
// OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
// SOFTWARE.

import ../../ReaKit/rk_svf.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/rk_svf_match.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/qz_engine.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/rk_srf.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/rk_theme.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/rk_menu.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/rk_curve.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/rk_spectrum.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/rk_gmem_link.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/rk_playstate.jsfx-inc
// the house knobs (ReaKit's knob library, as the 3-Band and GainKit draw theirs): simple mode's deck (the user, 2026-10-30:
// "they get ReaKit knobs, not just some random new knobs")
import ../../ReaKit/utils_kbsg.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/knobs_kbsg.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/knobs_kbsg_p2.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/knobs_kbsg_p3.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/knobs_kbsg_p4.jsfx-inc
// the ring ("Saturn") round the strip's four bells
import ../../ReaKit/rk_knob_ring.jsfx-inc
import ../../ReaKit/qz_face.jsfx-inc

// ---- Controls (spec §5; the layout locks at release 1: add only after slider 221, never between) ----
// Band b = sliders 13(b-1)+1 .. 13b: Mode, Place, Shape, Freq, Gain, Q, Slope, then the release-2 dynamics
// (Threshold, Ratio, Range, Attack, Release, Release sync), inert in release 1. EVERY control is hidden ('-'):
// the house shows no REAPER slider panel over a face (wiki 4.5 rule 6); the window edits them. 209-218 output section,
// 219 Link Group, 220-221 the theme panel's rows (a Quality slot was dropped with HQ, 2026-10-22: never released). Written by .dev_tests/quezy_gen_sliders.py: edit the table
// there and re-generate, never by hand.
// @@QZ_SLIDERS BEGIN (generated by .dev_tests/quezy_gen_sliders.py; do not edit by hand)
